    "title": "Indiana BMV recognizes Motorcycle Safety Awareness Month - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nHENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — The Indiana BMV is recognizing May as Motorcycle Safety Awareness Month.\nThis month the Bureau of Motor Vehicles and Ride Safe Indiana are stressing the importance of safety as riding season begins. Ride Safe Indiana is the state’s official motorcycle safety program.\nOfficials say the program trains motorcyclists and teaches them how to reduce crashes and fatalities. In 2024, there were nearly 3,000 crashes involving motorcycles.\nThat’s why Indiana officials are using this month to emphasize the need for proper training.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).\n1",
    "summary": "HENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — The Indiana BMV is recognizing May as Motorcycle Safety Awareness Month. This month the Bureau of Motor Vehicles and Ride Safe Indiana are stressing the importance of safety as riding season begins. Ride Safe Indiana is the state’s official motorcycle safety program. Officials say the program trains motorcyclists and teaches them how to reduce crashes and fatalities. That’s why Indiana officials are using this month to emphasize the need for proper training.",
